    },
    {
      "padding": 0,
      "lineHeight": 1.5,
      "id": "markdown-10",
      "kind": "text",
      "name": "When the last saved version was written by a different…",
      "text": "When the last saved version was written by a different member, Memory can reconcile wording and duplication in your change before it is applied. If two decisions contradict each other, it shows the contradiction instead of choosing one. Consecutive edits by the same member skip this step. Reconciliation and review are independent: a Junior’s change still needs approval either way.",
      "assetId": null,
